What is Dextranase?
Dextranase is a specialized enzyme derived from Bacillus licheniformis through submerged fermentation. As an endonuclease, it specifically cleaves α-1,3 and α-1,4 glycosidic bonds in dextran - a problematic polysaccharide that compromises product quality in various industries. By breaking down dextran into oligosaccharides and glucose, this versatile enzyme enhances processing efficiency in sugar production, brewing, and pharmaceutical manufacturing.

